-- reading --
   The tightest coupling is S6 -> S7, and the stage that
   runs out of batch tolerance first is S7 (+/- 0.331 kJ/mol alone).
   Every stage has the same leverage per kJ/mol, so this ranking comes
   from the measured Table 3 margins, not from any width we assigned.
   A batch interval wider than a tolerance above can remove the mid-
   plateau driving force of that coupling; whether the cascade then
   stalls depends on plateau slope and kinetics, which this file does
   not vary and mhhc_corner_pbox.sio carries as declared intervals.

